  "function": "suggested_mark",
  "note": "The mark a sponsor's report gives and a value beside the record, by hand (docs/08 section 12, rules 12.2 to 12.5), with a variance flag of 10%. Stake 1, worked example 4: E0 = 413,000,000 - 150,000,000 = 263,000,000 and E1 = 428,050,000 - 146,300,000 = 281,750,000, so S = 7,310,450.25 x 281,750,000 / 263,000,000 = 7,831,632.5396..., 7,831,632.54. Stake 2, worked example 6: 100.00 x 1,000,000 / 3,000,000 = 33.3333..., 33.33. Stake 3: 100.01 x 1 / 2 = 50.005, half a cent, rounds up to 50.01. Stake 4: an equity value of 263,000,000 at both ends gives back the mark. Stake 5: net cash, 100,000,000 + 20,000,000 = 120,000,000 = 110,000,000 + 10,000,000, gives back the mark. Stakes 6 to 15 are the reasons in their order, each with a later reason applying as well where one can: no reference mark; a cash flow since it; no reference figures (none at all, no enterprise value, no net debt); a reference equity value of zero and of -10,000,000; no new net debt; a new equity value of zero and of -6,300,000. Stake 16: a Locked mark of zero scales to zero, and stake 17: 1.00 x 1,000 / 263,000,000 is under half a cent: no value (value_not_positive). Held 1, worked example 5: EV1 = 43,900,000 x 413,000,000 / 41,300,000 = 439,000,000, E1 = 439,000,000 - 146,300,000 = 292,700,000, S = 7,310,450.25 x 292,700,000 / 263,000,000 = 8,136,002.9968..., 8,136,003.00. Held 2: EV1 = 31,000,000 x 400,000,000 / 30,000,000 = 413,333,333.33..., E1 = 318,333,333.33..., S = 1,000,000 x 318,333,333.33... / 300,000,000 = 1,061,111.11. Held 3: the same EBITDA and net debt give back the mark. Held 4 to 7: rule 12.2's first four reasons come first. Held 8 to 10: no EBITDA in the earlier quarter, none in the new one, and none in one quarter with one below zero in the other (no_ebitda is the first). Held 11 to 13: an EBITDA of zero or below it in either quarter. Held 14: no new net debt; the enterprise value held is still shown. Held 15: 14,630,000 x 10 = 146,300,000 leaves an equity value of exactly zero, and held 16 one of -46,300,000. Held 17: a Locked mark of zero. Comparison 1, worked example 1: 20,940,000 against 18,420,000, the previous quarter's mark, is +2,520,000, 13.68078176%, flagged; net of flows 20,940,000 - 18,420,000 - 2,000,000 + 350,000 = 870,000, 4.72312704%. Comparisons 2 to 4, worked examples 4, 5 and 6: +521,182.29 (7.12927757%, no flag); +825,552.75 (11.29277571%, flagged); -66.67 (-66.67% over the rounded value, flagged). Comparison 5: the same figures as 1 against a mark older than the previous quarter: the change stands, no flag, no net of flows. Comparison 6: no mark on record. Comparison 7: no suggested value. Comparisons 8 to 11: exactly +10% and exactly -10% are flagged; 10,999,999.99 against 10,000,000 is 0.099999999 and is not; 1,099,999,999.96 against 1,000,000,000 is 0.09999999996, travels as 0.1 and is flagged. Comparison 12: a statement whose beginning balance is 500,000 off the mark has no net of flows; 13: exactly the 25,000 tolerance away it has; 14: a cent beyond, it has not. Comparisons 15 to 17: no distributions, no contributions or no beginning balance stated: no net of flows. Comparison 18: against a mark of zero there is a change and no percent, and a net of flows (2,500,000 - 0 - 2,000,000 + 0 = 500,000) with no percent. Comparison 19: a net of flows of -3,070,000, a change of -7.7%, not flagged. Cross-check 1, worked example 7: 7,831,632.54 against 7,810,000.00 is +21,632.54, 0.27698515%: the sources do not differ. Cross-checks 2 to 4: 8,591,000 is exactly 10% above and 7,029,000 exactly 10% below (both differ); 7,029,000.01 is a hair inside (they do not). Cross-checks 5 to 7: a source with no value, a suggestion with none, and the same value.",
